# CNS LINE OA

LINE HMAC `POST /webhook` and `POST /webhook/:channelId` (and `POST /webhook-alt` when `LINE_SECOND_WEBHOOK`) → identity SoR → one `resolveCommandReply` → Flex.
GraphQL `ingestLineEvents` (`GRAPHQL_LINE_INGEST`, ops-auth) is an allowed ingest path → `processLineMessageJob` → the same `resolveCommandReply`. Do not duplicate command logic.
`MONGO_USERS` on: Mongo is identity SoR (Firestore may mirror). Odoo masters stay in Odoo via `getErpAdapter()` — never Mongo as Odoo SoR.
Non-odoo `ERP_PROVIDER` values use an unimplemented placeholder adapter (fail closed). Do not implement SAP/QuickBooks/Oracle RPC.

Admin chain (fail closed): LINE id → profile (SoR) → `odooVerified` → `ADMIN_USER_ID` → Odoo admin capability → `role=admin`.

## Environments

| `APP_ENV` | Host | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `development` | laptop | Local + `/webhook-test` + `/demo` |
| `staging` | Railway | Demo; set ENABLE_* flags; `NODE_ENV=production` |
| `production` | final delivery | Demo and webhook-test off even if ENABLE_* is set |

Unset `APP_ENV` with `NODE_ENV=production` is treated as production.

Optional adapters (Swagger, GraphQL ingest, Mongo identity when flagged, Mongo RAG, BullMQ) share the same command processor. Production deploy is a separate cut.

